.\" SPDX-License-Identifier: BSD-3-Clause
.Dd October 18, 2026
.Dt GROUPMOD 8
.Os OxideBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm groupmod
.Nd change a group
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl ov
.Op Fl g Ar gid
.Op Fl n Ar newname
.Ar group
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility changes
.Ar group
in
.Pa /etc/group ,
in the shape of the
.Nx
and
.Ox
command.
It is
.Xr pw 8
under another name; its
.Cm groupmod
command also changes the member list.
It must be run by the superuser.
.Pp
The options are as follows:
.Bl -tag -width "-n newname"
.It Fl g Ar gid
The new group ID.
Users whose primary group it was keep the old ID.
.It Fl n Ar newname
The new name.
.It Fl o
Allow a group ID already in use.
.It Fl v
Say what was done.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
As
.Xr pw 8 .
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr group 5 ,
.Xr groupadd 8 ,
.Xr groupdel 8 ,
.Xr pw 8
.Sh HISTORY
A
.Nm
utility appeared in
.Nx 1.5
and
.Ox 2.7 .
This implementation was written for OxideBSD.
